lessons.body:
Designers of furniture, vehicles, jewellery and games combine polynomial curves. For a design report, include for each function you use:

* the equation, domain and range, and end behaviour;
* the value of the constant finite differences;
* any transformations used and any symmetry;
* connections to average and instantaneous rates of change (e.g. how steep an edge is at a point).

Example: the top of a bench backrest could be $y = -0.02(x - 5)^4 + 6$, $0 \le x \le 10$ — even power, vertex $(5, 6)$, symmetric about $x = 5$, fourth differences constant at $-0.02 \times 24 = -0.48$.

